## 7. What is missing or needs strengthening

The existing Alo King product specification already includes strong safeguards: organic recommendations separated from sponsored placement, no pay-to-win organic ranking, sponsored labels, opt-out handling, merchant-specific audiences, frequency caps, moderation, payment-ledger requirements, attribution, and pilot kill gates.

The following items are still needed or should be strengthened.

### P0 — Before selling campaigns

#### 1. Persistent memory schema

Create dedicated structures such as:

```text
customer_preferences
customer_preference_events
customer_feedback
customer_recommendation_impressions
customer_recommendation_actions
customer_suppression_rules
```

Each preference needs a source, confidence, timestamp, and deletion behavior.

#### 2. Memory correction and deletion

Support:

```text
Forget that
Remove my preferences
What do you remember about me?
I do not like spicy food anymore
```

The customer should be able to view, correct, delete, or disable personalization.

#### 3. Recommendation feedback loop

Add feedback options such as:

```text
More like this
Not interested
Too expensive
Too far
I ordered this before
Show different restaurants
```

#### 4. Campaign attribution model

Connect:

```text
campaign
→ recipient
→ delivery status
→ reply
→ cart
→ order
→ completed delivery
→ revenue
```

Use campaign IDs and pseudonymous recipient IDs. Never expose customer phone numbers to merchants.

#### 5. Holdouts and experiments

Use a small control group to determine whether campaigns create incremental orders rather than merely receiving credit for orders that would have happened anyway.

#### 6. Complete cost accounting

The merchant price must account for Meta delivery charges, service replies, AI/API usage, failed-message refunds, payment processing, support cost, and discounts or credits.

### P1 — For a genuinely intelligent bot

#### 7. Explicit conversation state machine

Do not rely on the LLM to remember workflow state. Store:

```text
intent
order_id
campaign_id
cart_id
current_step
pending_confirmation
last_question
confidence
handoff_status
```

#### 8. Customer-level experimentation

Measure whether recommendations improve conversion, average order value, reorder rate, satisfaction, and cancellation rate.

#### 9. Recommendation diversity and fairness

Track exposure, provide controlled new-merchant exploration, limit restaurant fatigue, maintain category diversity, and keep paid placement separate from organic ranking.

#### 10. Merchant campaign quality score

Score each merchant using delivery rate, reply rate, opt-outs, blocks/reports, complaints, completed orders, and refunds. Automatically reduce or pause campaign access when quality deteriorates.

#### 11. Lebanese Arabic evaluation set

Test Lebanese Arabic, Arabizi, English switching, voice notes, spelling mistakes, village names, restaurant names, food slang, quantities, numbers, and ambiguous modifiers.

### P2 — Advanced capabilities

Later add send-time optimization, product propensity models, restaurant similarity, personalized bundles, churn prediction, customer lifetime value, campaign budget optimization, multi-armed bandits, loyalty personalization, referral optimization, voice-note ordering, group-order memory, and diaspora gift-order personalization.

