## 8. Recommended architecture

```text
WhatsApp message
        ↓
Webhook validation + idempotency
        ↓
Intent and language detection
        ↓
Conversation state lookup
        ↓
Customer memory retrieval
        ↓
Hard safety / availability / consent filters
        ↓
Deterministic tools:
  menu, price, availability, delivery, order, campaign, profile
        ↓
Recommendation or campaign ranker
        ↓
LLM response wording
        ↓
Confirmation gate for money/order/send actions
        ↓
Persist event + send WhatsApp reply
        ↓
Measure outcome
```

The LLM must not directly invent menu prices, decide whether a restaurant is open, send a campaign without confirmation, override allergy constraints, choose a paid ranking position, expose customer data, issue credits, or approve its own moderation exception.

---

## 9. Priority implementation order

### 1. Customer Memory v1

Structured preferences, reorder history, corrections, deletion, confidence, and recency decay.

### 2. Recommendation Engine v1

Hard constraints first, personalized ranking second, explainable reasons, feedback buttons, and no paid influence.

### 3. Campaign Engine v1

Objective-based campaign creation, consent-safe audience selection, preview, payment confirmation, moderation, pacing, holdout measurement, attribution, and automatic pause rules.

Once reliable, Alo King can become a personal food concierge for customers and a measurable revenue engine for Lebanese restaurants.
